  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Mourillon beaches cover more than 40 hectares, 19 of them dedicated to swimming, with four coves (Lido, Mistral, de la Source, des Pins) and the Tabarly cove devoted to water sports, where swimming is prohibited (city of Toulon). The site has 1,300 free parking spaces.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The latest order published by the city of Toulon (AR/PM/2026/02, dated 28 September 2026, which repeals the orders of 26 June 2025 and 12 May 2026) allows leashed pets, notably dogs, to move around year-round on the public Mourillon beaches site, except on the sand, lawns, playgrounds and sports facilities. The Henri-Fabre promenade has been open to dogs on a leash since May 2026. Category 1 and 2 dogs must also be muzzled. Any offence is punishable by a 2nd-class fine of up to €150.</p>
      <p>Two types of dog areas complete the setup: two "dog parks" between the car park and the beaches (one for small dogs, the other for larger ones, according to the city) and a year-round "dog beach" on the peninsula by the Tabarly cove, with a pontoon for getting into the water.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the rules were changed in 2025 and twice in 2026 — a glance at the signage at the site entrance remains the best guarantee. The city also asks that no soap or shampoo be used in the showers.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>To let your dog run or swim, see the <a href="/en/fiche-anse-tabarly-toulon">Tabarly cove dog beach</a> and the <a href="/en/fiche-pipady-toulon">Pipady dog beach</a>, at the foot of the Tour Royale.</p>
    </div>

